│ Okay, let’s address this. Based on the repeated feedback and the   │
│ final successful retrieval of the code snippet, the issue is about │
│ ensuring that the required attribute isn't displayed on the HTML   │
│ input element for FileInput when a file is already selected. The   │
│ core of the fix lies within                                        │
│ ClearableFileInput.use_required_attribute(), which is incorrectly  │
│ applying the required attribute even when a file is already        │
│ associated with the form.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The use_required_attribute() method in ClearableFileInput          │
│ currently sets the required attribute on the underlying HTML input │
│ element. This is undesirable when a file has already been          │
│ selected, as it creates unnecessary validation and a confusing     │
│ user experience. The fix involves conditionally removing the       │
│ required attribute only when a file is present.                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Patch:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # modification 1                                                  │
│  [file]django/forms/widgets.py[/file]                              │
│  [original] def use_required_attribute(self, attrs):               │
│      attrs = self.add_attrs(attrs)                                 │
│      if self.required:                                             │
│          attrs['required'] = 'required'                            │
│      return attrs[/original]                                       │
│  [patched] def use_required_attribute(self, attrs):                │
│      attrs = self.add_attrs(attrs)                                 │
│      if self.required and self.file_field.data:                    │
│          attrs['required'] = ''                                    │
│      return attrs[/patched]                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explanation:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The patch adds a conditional check within                          │
│ use_required_attribute(). It now only sets the required attribute  │
│ to 'required' if both self.required is True and                    │
│ self.file_field.data is not None (meaning a file has been          │
│ selected). If either of these conditions is false, the required    │
│ attribute is not set, effectively removing it from the HTML input  │
│ element.  I've assumed self.file_field is the field that holds the │
│ file data within ClearableFileInput.                               │
